{"kind":"request","text":"BO2: views as notes. Second slice of the boundary-objects design note (notes/2026-10-28-boundary-objects-in-use.md, section 9, landed 25930f62), child of request bc4aa093. Replaces 13f354c0, which described the note's first version. After BO1, and after declared views reach the generic server and the hosted endpoint.\n\nScope, as the note's slice list states it:\n1. The host lists a room's views from notes whose text is a declaration in the form of the chat-composed views note. A note by the same signer, in the same media type, about an earlier declaration is a revision, and the newest is current.\n2. Built-in views over notes with no declaration: a thread, a table over notes whose text is data, a timeline, an image with regions, and two versions of a text side by side. A declaration adds a shape or a column to one of them. A column may be an expression over the sources in the restricted@1 profile the view session compiles filters to; an expression reads notes and writes nothing.\n3. Sources by reference and fragment: notes and documents, and a package's projections. The host mounts a view for a member over the rooms that member reads; a source in a room the member does not read appears as unreadable with the room named and nothing else shown. A view in a shared room names a private note by its fact reference and never by the digest of its text. Two views that name the same references are views of one thing, and the host says so.\n4. The person edits a declaration in the generic interface; the edit is a new note about the old.\n5. A view may write any act its member may sign. The host shows the exact act to the member, signs it on the member's action alone, and refuses an act the member's grants or memberships do not allow, and the view shows the refusal. A mark from a view is a note about a reference with a fragment.\n6. Witness W2 (one list, two views), as the note's table states it, including B's mark written from B's view and B's refused note in A's own room.\n\nNot in this slice: the install screen's slot list (BO3), the matter view (BO4), views as code (BO5).","body":{"conditions":"Views listed and mounted from notes; built-in thread, table, timeline, image and versions views over notes; declarations with sources by reference and fragment and restricted@1 columns that write nothing; view editing writes a new note about the old; unreadable sources name the room only; private notes by fact reference never text digest; a view writes any act the member may sign, shown first, signed on the member's action, refused beyond grants; witness W2 recorded with the mark from the view and the refused note; gate green.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}